# Line endings: LF on every platform. The drift check hashes file
# bytes against a manifest recorded on Linux; with no rule here, a
# Windows checkout converts LF to CRLF, so every text file's bytes
# differ and the check reports them all 'drifted' (CI 0.9.4, windows
# job: 129 drifted — every file with a newline; the one survivor was
# the empty __init__.py, which has no line endings to convert).
# text=auto only applies to files git detects as text, so binary
# files are unaffected.
* text=auto eol=lf
